  "id": "guangdong_hanyue",
  "name": "Guangdong hanyue (Hakka Han music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Instrumental ensemble music of the Hakka of Meizhou and Dabu in eastern Guangdong, traditionally said to preserve music brought south by Han migrants from the Central Plains and listed as national intangible heritage; wind-and-percussion bands serve rites and festivals. Its intimate sixian (silk-string) ensemble is led by the high touxian fiddle with the Hakka zheng (here the guzheng card), yangqin, pipa, sanxian and other fiddles, sometimes with the dongxiao (here the xiao card) and small percussion.",
  "recipe": "classic modern guangdong hanyue, art Music, east Asian branch. high pitched ensemble lead touxian, wutong paulownia guzheng, intimate traditional yangqin, pipa, sanxian, xiao. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
